<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs close mostly firmer, Dow ends at record.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs close mostly firmer, Dow ends at record.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs closed mostly firmer in late New York while the Dow gained 47.39 points to a record closing high of 7,333.55.</p>
<p>Company		   Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail   N.Y.    US$27 3/4	 -0 1/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$32 1/4	 +0 7/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$32 1/4	 +0 7/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	 N.Y.    US$22 1/2	   nil  *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13 1/4	 +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$36		 nil  *</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.28		-4</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.52		+3</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  A$3.15		-5</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of eight shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
